{
    "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
    "annotation": "Build SWISS-MODEL homology models for all sequences of a multi-FASTA file, filter models by GMQE threshold and build structure-based trees with FoldTree.",
    "comments": [],
    "creator": [
        {
            "class": "Person",
            "identifier": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9673-9103",
            "name": "Stefan Bienert"
        }
    ],
    "doi": [
        "https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gky427",
        "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41594-025-01649-8"
    ],
    "format-version": "0.1",
    "help": "## Before you run\n\n- **FASTA headers become names.** Each header is used to name the per-sequence results and, with special characters replaced by `_`, the leaves of the trees. Keep headers short and make sure every header is unique.\n- **Project title** is optional. Use it to find the SWISS-MODEL projects and the model collections in your history later.\n\n## Reading the results\n\n- Start with **Models passing GMQE filter**. It shows which models made it into the trees and their GMQE values.\n- The **FoldTree metric tree** is the main result. Compare it with the **TM-score tree** and **LDDT tree**: branches supported by all three are more reliable.\n- All models, including those that failed the filter, are kept in **Model PDB files** and **Model metadata**.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n- **FoldTree fails or produces no tree:** check **Models passing GMQE filter**. FoldTree needs at least two structures; if fewer models pass, there is nothing to build a tree from.\n- **A sequence has no models:** SWISS-MODEL found no suitable template for it, or the modelling job failed. Open the failed job's details to see the message from SWISS-MODEL.\n- **Fewer models than expected in the trees:** models with a GMQE below the provided threshold are removed. The threshold is set in the step \"Filter by GMQE\".",
    "license": "BSD-3-Clause",
    "name": "SWISS-MODEL to FoldTree",
    "readme": "# SWISS-MODEL to FoldTree\n\nBuilds homology models for a set of protein sequences with SWISS-MODEL, keeps only the models of sufficient quality and builds structure-based trees from them with FoldTree.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- **Project title** (optional): used as the SWISS-MODEL project title and in the names of the model collections. If left empty, SWISS-MODEL uses \"Untitled project\".\n- **Multi-FASTA file**: the protein sequences to model, one FASTA record per target.\n\n## What happens\n\n1. The multi-FASTA file is split into one dataset per sequence.\n2. SWISS-MODEL (automodel) builds homology models for each sequence. This calls the SWISS-MODEL API, so runtime depends on the SWISS-MODEL server.\n3. The GMQE value of each model is read from its metadata, and only models with GMQE of at least the provided threshold are kept.\n4. The PDB files of all passing models are collected into one list and passed to FoldTree.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- **Model PDB files** and **Model metadata**: all SWISS-MODEL results, grouped by sequence.\n- **Models passing GMQE filter**: table of the models that passed (sequence, model, GMQE).\n- **FoldTree metric tree**, **TM-score tree**, **LDDT tree**: Newick trees of the passing models. The FoldTree metric tree is the main result; the other two are for comparison.\n\n## Notes and limitations\n\n- Tree leaf names are built from the FASTA headers and model names. Characters such as `|`, `:` and spaces are replaced by `_`.\n- FoldTree needs at least two structures. If fewer than two models pass the filter, no tree can be built.\n- FoldTree's own pLDDT filter is switched off, because SWISS-MODEL PDB files do not contain AlphaFold pLDDT values.\n",
    "report": {
        "markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n\r\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\r\n"
    },
